## Local (your GPU)

1. Copy `.env.example` to `.env` and fill in the keys.
2. Open the folder in VS Code and choose **Reopen in Container**.
3. Inside the container:

```bash
make doctor        # image smoke test + GPU visible? (also runs on container start)
make train-smoke   # seconds-long sanity check
make test
make train         # torchrun across all local GPUs, configs/default.yaml
make train ARGS="lr=1e-3 run_name=lr1e-3"
```

Host mounts: `{{ host_data_dir }}` → `/workspace/data`, `{{ host_cache_dir }}` → `/workspace/.cache`.

## Cloud (SkyPilot)

One-time: `sky check` to see which clouds are enabled (credentials in `~/.aws`, `~/.config/gcloud`, RunPod/Lambda API keys, etc.).
Create the bucket `{{ bucket_uri }}` with `data/` and `checkpoints/` prefixes.

```bash
make sky-train                                       # managed spot job, auto-resumes on preemption
sky jobs launch sky/train.yaml --env RUN_NAME=exp2 --gpus H100:8 --secret WANDB_API_KEY
make sky-dev                                         # interactive GPU box, same dev image
make sky-status
```

Checkpoints land in `{{ bucket_uri }}/checkpoints/<run_name>/`. Relaunching with the same `RUN_NAME` resumes.

## Layout

| Path | What |
|---|---|
| `src/{{ package_name }}/train.py` | DDP training loop, AMP, SIGTERM-safe checkpointing, resume |
| `src/{{ package_name }}/model.py` | **Replace:** toy model and synthetic data |
| `configs/*.yaml` | Run configs; override any key with `key=value` |
| `sky/train.yaml`, `sky/dev.yaml` | Cloud job / dev box definitions |
| `.devcontainer/` | Local GPU container |

## Dependencies

torch/CUDA come locked from the base image. Add project deps to `pyproject.toml`, then `make install`;
installs use `-c $MAI_CONSTRAINTS` so they can never change the image's torch version.

## Base image updates

{% if image_version -%}
This project pins `{{ image_repo }}` release **{{ image_version }}** (`dev-{{ image_version }}` locally,
`runtime-{{ image_version }}` in the cloud and CI). With the [Renovate app](https://github.com/apps/renovate)
installed on this repo, a newer mai-base release arrives as one PR that bumps every reference together:
`.devcontainer/compose.yaml`, `sky/*.yaml` and `.github/workflows/ci.yml`. CI runs your tests on the new image
before you merge. After merging, rebuild the devcontainer to pick it up locally.
{%- else -%}
This project floats on the rolling `dev` / `runtime` tags, so it always gets the newest mai-base build
(re-pull with *Dev Containers: Rebuild Container*). To pin a release instead: `uvx copier update --data image_version=0.1.0`.
{%- endif %}

## Template updates

```bash
uvx copier update      # pulls newer mai-platform template changes, 3-way merges with yours
```
